=== 12b. periphery, corrected
The step above reported 0 because the cached build carried no index store: periphery failed with
`Error: index store path does not exist: .../Sources/.build/debug/index/store` and the script had
discarded stderr. Re-run from a clean build with the flag:

  rm -rf Sources/.build
  swift build --package-path Sources --build-tests --enable-index-store
  periphery scan --project-root Sources --retain-public --format csv

  findings: 23
  unused:   0        (all assignOnlyProperty — value-record fields periphery cannot attribute to
                      the synthesized ==/hash, the same set the 2026-09-13 audit retained)

NOTE for scripts/check-format.sh-style automation: `--enable-index-store` on a *cached* SwiftPM
build does not regenerate the store, because nothing is recompiled. The store only appears when the
build actually runs, so a clean scratch directory (or removing Sources/.build) is required.
